      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's influence on social realist cinema cannot be overstated. Its raw depiction of economic hardship and moral compromise set the template for Italian Neorealism, particularly visible in **Germany Year Zero** (1948) and **Umberto D.** (1952). The careful attention to women's experiences in times of social crisis influenced later feminist filmmakers, from Agnès Varda to Chantal Akerman."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Pabst's innovative camera techniques, particularly his use of close-ups to capture psychological turmoil, influenced the development of dramatic realism in European cinema. This approach can be traced through works like **La Strada** (1954) and **L'Avventura** (1960), where character psychology drives the narrative. SUBHEAD: Impact on Social Cinema"
      },
